{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963274-kinfolk-gifts","id":963274,"title":"Kinfolk Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-04T11:01:15-07:00","id":963274,"title":"Kinfolk Gifts","content":"So, I was looking at the Kinfolk Gifts from Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, and I realized that the Kinfolk Gifts were quite good forms of magic. For example, Eve's Touch, allows you to roll Intelligence plus Medicine, difficult 6, and heal one health levels of non-aggravated damage per two successes. The only restriction is one use per day per person. Since they can be used by Garou, do you ever have anyone using them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:13:22-07:00","id":963322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963274-kinfolk-gifts#post963274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was looking at the Kinfolk Gifts from Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, and I realized that the Kinfolk Gifts were quite good forms of magic. For example, Eve's Touch, allows you to roll Intelligence plus Medicine, difficult 6, and heal one health levels of non-aggravated damage per two successes. The only restriction is one use per day per person. Since they can be used by Garou, do you ever have anyone using them?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very much inferior to Mother's Touch, imo.<br /> <br /> I've used kinfolk gifts before, but they are generally weaker than normal Garou gifts (under most circumstances). And I take the ones written as suggestions and make up my own. Only very rare and extraordinary kinfolk ever end up with gifts anyways. They are far more likely to have a few dots of hedge magic, which is likewise rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T17:25:59-07:00","id":963461,"title":"","content":"Mother's Touch requires Gnosis, but I see no reason why a dedicated healer cannot learn both, since Eve's Touch would allow you to help out Kinfolk without spending Gnosis..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T17:46:44-07:00","id":963470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963274-kinfolk-gifts?p=963461#post963461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mother's Touch requires Gnosis, but I see no reason why a dedicated healer cannot learn both, since Eve's Touch would allow you to help out Kinfolk without spending Gnosis..</div> </div> </div> </div>I have had characters use that gift for that reason. I had a Child of Gaia in a previous game who knew the gift so that he didn't need to use Mother's touch on non-shifters who had an injury. It was his way of not having to waste a Gnosis when he didn't have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T18:54:30-07:00","id":963480,"title":"","content":"Personally, I feel that is too munchkiny (for games I run or played in). Anyone worth healing is worth spending the Gnosis on. And Garou almost always have to heal each other anyways, so it would be far too situational for my tastes anyways.<br /> Since I'm used to Gifts being actual legwork to learn (chiminage in addition to the XP), it just doesn't seem worth it. That's just me though. The Gift would also be out of tribe/breed/auspice which makes it even harder to convince a Spirit to teach it to a Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T02:54:14-07:00","id":963612,"title":"","content":"Oddly enough, I could see Get of Fenris learning this before Children of Gaia. CoG kin would tend toward less violent lifestyles, while the GoF have an entire Kinfolk society of mercs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T06:41:36-07:00","id":963665,"title":"","content":"Heck, I could see them teaching it to their Kinfolk medics. A medic that could heal an average of one health level of lethal damage per day per person would be worth their weight on gold for a mercenary outfit, as they could take someone from Incapacitated to Bruised in just a week, rather than the eleven months of healing that it would normally take. A Garou medic could probably heal two health levels of lethal damage per day per person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T11:54:44-07:00","id":963820,"title":"","content":"A Garou medic (aka one that's done more than pick up Mother's Touch and is actually focused on healing more than that), can heal a lot more than 2L per person per day; esp. if you're willing to allow some customized Rites and Talens/Fetishes. Going to Eve's Touch seems to be treating Mother's Touch as the only healing stuff you can do. There's plenty of more Gnosis efficient options out there.<br /> <br /> As well, a Kin that has access to Numina can use one of the healing Paths and be way more effective than Eve's Touch (even if it comes with the issue of Numina use over Gift use).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T15:01:06-07:00","id":963931,"title":"","content":"No, not really. Numina healing is much slower than one health level of lethal damage per turn. The Healing 4 only doubles healing rate for lethal damage and requires 1 Willpower per injury, so it can only be used a couple of times per day. Psychic Healing 4 is more effective, but it costs 1 Willpower per use, so it can only be used a couple of times a day. If you want large scale healing, Eye's Touch is simply the best healing power in the classic WoD because it is fast, does not require a Gnosis roll, and costs nothing to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T17:16:52-07:00","id":963982,"title":"","content":"And it still doesn't make any sense to learn in setting.<br /> <br /> That is my biggest problem with the idea of Garou learning kinfolk gifts. How does that negotiation go with the spirit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T18:00:58-07:00","id":963995,"title":"","content":"Lethal healing is not good; sometimes you will need to fix up injured friends and family, but that should be the exception, not the rule. Garou regenerate lethal damage on their own, and kinfolk or mundane humans aren't capable of combating serious threats. Humans are too squishy to depend on in the last days of Gaia.<br /> <br /> All of this ignores the social problems and logistics of a Garou playing medic to humans (with kinfolk gifts, no less). Such a thing is back-asswards, and I think the spirits would laugh. That is like a marine refusing to fight in wartime and instead going off to give bandaids to boy-scouts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T18:52:16-07:00","id":964009,"title":"","content":"The Kinfolk book specifically says that Garou can learn Kinfolk Gifts. And we are talking about the Get of Fenris Kinfolk mercenary units. People in combat take damage and having someone that can instantly stabilize someone with critical injuries is invaluable in combat. A Children of Gaia trauma doctor could also find use for the gift because it would be considered unwise to use Gnosis to save humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T19:09:40-07:00","id":964015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963274-kinfolk-gifts?p=963995#post963995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of this ignores the social problems and logistics of a Garou playing medic to humans (with kinfolk gifts, no less). Such a thing is back-asswards, and I think the spirits would laugh. That is like a marine refusing to fight in wartime and instead going off to give bandaids to boy-scouts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. So much this.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter that on pure mechanics this seems like a good option. It makes zero sense in setting. Learning Eve's Touch would be a waste of valuable time for most any Garou.<br /> Like I said, any kinfolk worth healing is worth spending a Gnosis on. This applies to humans too. I just don't see a Garou using this much.<br /> <br /> There are problems even learning the gift. Then you have to dedicate yourself to healing humans which means overcoming the a Curse and going against your Divine purpose.<br /> The very situational and completely mechanical benefits (which are debatable) don't outweigh the setting fluff.<br /> <br /> A Garou should never feel the need to go out a learn kinfolk gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T19:11:35-07:00","id":964017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963274-kinfolk-gifts?p=964009#post964009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kinfolk book specifically says that Garou can learn Kinfolk Gifts. And we are talking about the Get of Fenris Kinfolk mercenary units. People in combat take damage and having someone that can instantly stabilize someone with critical injuries is invaluable in combat. A Children of Gaia trauma doctor could also find use for the gift because it would be considered unwise to use Gnosis to save humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that a reason for those kinfolk to learn the kinfolk gift?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T20:06:43-07:00","id":964033,"title":"","content":"It is a reason for anyone to learn Kinfolk Gifts. Each of the three in the Kinfolk book are quite useful. Echoes, for example, would allow you to listen to conversations hours or days after they have occured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:11:56-07:00","id":964055,"title":"","content":"Echoes makes the most sense to learn, and the least sense to be a kinfolk gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T13:36:20-07:00","id":964501,"title":"","content":"I do not know. Its utility is limited to espionage, and Kinfolk are much better for espionage than Garou. It would have also been developed hundreds or thousands of years ago, when espionage was much less sophisticated than in modern times. In 1000 AD, listening into a lord's conversations after they occurred may have been good military intelligence, but it would not have allowed you become a lord. In 2000 AD, listen into a CEO's conversations after they occurred can allow you to become a millionaire or even a billionaire because you would have phenomenal inside information (which would make masquerading as a janitor worth the hassle).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:46:33-07:00","id":964730,"title":"","content":"Neither here nor there, but I disagree with a few points.<br /> I certainly disagree that kinfolk are better at espionage. On Gifts alone they are far better over a dozen Gifts come to mind). Then add spirits, Talens and Fetishes, shapeshifting (heightened senses that come with it), Umbral travel (as well as Peeking). There is no comparison. It's why the Glasswalkers monkeywrench and don't leave it to their kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Second point that the Gift (Echoes) was developed &quot;hundreds or thousands of years ago&quot; is completely unfounded. There is no way to tell when any Gift was developed, so this is a complete guess. And listening to a lord's conversation could very well have allowed you to become Lord, depending on who you are. This sounds like a better argument for Echoes being a Shadow Lord gift than anything.<br /> <br /> I think the whole idea of Kinfolk Gifts wasn't terribly thought out (supported by there being only 3 printed, to my knowledge). And the fact that they should be incredibly rare is just kind of glossed over for the sake of conversations like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:06:43-07:00","id":964754,"title":"","content":"No, Kinfolk Gifts are not rare, you just cannot purchase them during character creation (unless you are using the Croatan Song rules). It is rare for Kinfolk to have more than a couple of Gifts, but there is no indication of Kinfolk with Gifts being particularly rare (neither the word rare or uncommon is used in either Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes or Croatan Song in reference to Kinfolk Gifts). Kinfolk with Gnosis, however, are quite rare, though how rare is up to the ST (I make them as rare as the Changing Breeds which, at 1:100,000 of the human population, is quite rare indeed). And the reason why Kinfolk are better at espionage is that they a) are less noticeable than Garou because they lack Rage and b) are better suited to non-combat roles than Garou because they are not superhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:56:53-07:00","id":964784,"title":"","content":"I don't think we read the same section in the Kinfolk book if you come away from that with the thought that Kinfolk with Gifts are somehow not rare. It says: &quot;how many might a mere kinfolk possess? Perhaps one, if he's lucky, maybe two if he's incredibly talented and worthy.&quot; That sounds rare (if you are being picky about wording, maybe &quot;uncommon&quot;?. I don;t remember what the statistical requirements are for each word). And then the cost is somewhere between 15 and 25 experience depending on circumstances. The cost alone prohibits Kinfolk from getting multiple gifts, never mind the tons of RP, deeds and renown go into earning just 1 Gift.<br /> I do agree that Gnosis is more rare than Gifts, but that doesn't have much to do with this.<br /> <br /> On the espionage thing, kinfolk might slip through masses unnoticed because of the lack of Rage (minimal Rage Garou can do the same, Ragabash are most likely to fill this role), but Garou can circumvent masses in general and go straight to what they need. In the example of using the Gift Echoes in a CEO's room, a Garou has a much easier way of getting there (1 night, through the Umbra) than working their way up the tedious corporate ladder to get access (months?). Homid Garou (most especially Glasswalkers) are going to be far better with computers and retrieving information in general (thanks to Gifts and Spirits).<br /> I'm not sure what your point is about Kinfolk somehow being better by <i>not</i> being superhuman. Garou are good at combat by default. Because of that, they can specialize in another area (espionage for example) and still be combat monsters all the same. I'm not sure how being superhuman is a negative here. And I'm not being sarcastic, I'm actually curious why you think it is.<br /> <br /> Edit: I didn't know there were other Kinfolk creation rules hidden in Croatan Song. I looked up that section and it doesn't really do anything to change what's already written in Unsung Heroes. It really just adds ST fiat to allow a kinfolk character to pay 15 freebies for a rank 1 Gift. Considering that that is more costly than 2 dots of numina (and requires special permission to even consider buying), I would still see that as rare.<br /> I am hoping the new Kinfolk book elaborates on a lot of this. It would be interesting to have them portray kinfolk as being more competent/useful in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-07-2016, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:28:53-07:00","id":964852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963274-kinfolk-gifts?p=964730#post964730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a better argument for Echoes being a Shadow Lord gift than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather have the actual Shadow Lord Gift Whisper Catching. Sure, you can't use it after the fact, but it's automatic with 1 WP, and has a range of 200 feet for perfect hearing of any whispered conversations around you. A Ragabash Shadow Lord spy that can't get within 200 feet of an important conversation shouldn't have been made Cliath.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T04:03:54-07:00","id":968445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963274-kinfolk-gifts?p=964754#post964754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Kinfolk Gifts are not rare, you just cannot purchase them during character creation (unless you are using the Croatan Song rules).</div> </div> </div> </div>They kind of are rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kinfolk Unsung Heros - page 54</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a highranking Theurge, such as Glass Walker Roger Daly, has 10 Gifts, while the Cliath Stargazer Galliard Howard Koar has three, how many might a mere Kinfolk possess? Perhaps one, if he\u2019s lucky, maybe two if he\u2019s incredibly talented or worthy. For Kin to possess Gifts \u2014 period \u2014 a good rationale needs to be in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another prerequisite is good roleplaying, so I'd like to see that happen to a NPC, that is a background character....<br /> <br /> I agree that &quot;Echos&quot; is the most powerful of the Kinfolk gifts, for it is an excellent spy tool. 'Eve's Touch' is not that powerful if you run a werewolf game, but it becomes more useful, in an all-Kinfolk game.<br /> <br /> And, keep in mind, that garou do not mass teach gifts between themselves or to kin. Gifts are given by spirits, not necessarily taught, but bestowed. Spirits can inherently sense a persons renown and therefore decide if they are willing to bestow a gift and if there is a need of compensation or offering for their blessing. Besides practical difficulties teaching a gift to another garou is usually dishonourable. W20 talks about defying tradition. I think Axis Mundi stated, that secrecy about the gift was a standard part of the things a spirit requests (Axis Mundi isn't part of my PDF library, so I can't check right now).<br /> <br /> So, a kin person can only get a gift through good role-playing and character development. That is a huge threshold. Sure, you can always define that your NPCs meet the requirements, but that is kind of circumventing the issue.<br /> Also, 15 XP is a lot. Per chapter, there is 1 XP auto, one for learning, one for acting, one for concept and one for heroism. So a character would have to play at least three chapters for the XP, however I find it hard to believe that one gets all of those. And NPCs usually don't get chapters, at all. So unless you play an all kin chronicle, the chances are, that NPCs don't even get enough XP to by a gift, aside from normal stats increases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:37:48-07:00","id":968854,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that a politcally savvy Garou like say a Shadowlord or Glasswalker could rack up a lot of secret favors by doing things like curing incurable diseases and performing supposedly impossible surgery by using Healing Gifts, Rites, and Fetishes. I mean the Hunter chapter fiction had a hunter starting up a cult by healing... so a Garou could very much do something similar with their much more flexible healing options. Curing a Prison Wardens Wife of an inoperable Tumor, Healing a Billionaire after severe Chemo killed his cancer, these are the type of things that can really help stack the deck in your fights against Pentex, or covering up the Veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:40:07-07:00","id":968855,"title":"","content":"And you can hide it as 'alternative medicine'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:32:28-07:00","id":971675,"title":"","content":"Oh on the Get of Fenris kin Society of Mercs I had an idea for a kinfolk fellowship in the Dark ages over a decade ago &quot;The Knights of the silver moon&quot; Largely Silver Fang, and Shadow Lord Kinfolk, with a scattering other tribes.<br /> <br /> though their willing to fight besides their Garou Family, Their focused more on keeping an ear to high society , and helping Garou of Lupus birth (though never as of yet Metis) or simply of low born human origin, establish themselves, amongst the nobility,if they can demonstrate their worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}